---
/**
 * Every analytics tag on the site, in one place.
 *
 * Previously this block was copy-pasted into four <head>s — Layout.astro,
 * quote.astro, get-started/[...slug].astro and associations/[slug].astro — so a
 * tag change meant four edits and any missed one silently stopped reporting.
 * Adding GA4 was the point at which that became worth fixing.
 *
 * ── gtag.js is loaded ONCE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * GA4 and Google Ads share the same library. The correct pattern is one
 * gtag/js request followed by a `config` call per measurement ID, NOT two
 * script tags. Two requests would download the same library twice and race to
 * initialize the same dataLayer.
 *
 * ── window.gtag must be global ────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Application code (constants.ts `trackLead`) calls `window.gtag`. An earlier
 * version kept gtag inside module scope, so every event call silently did
 * nothing. The consent loader assigns `window.gtag` explicitly for that reason.
 *
 * ── Consent first ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Google Analytics runs unless the visitor declines it; Microsoft Clarity and
 * Google Ads wait until the visitor allows them in the privacy banner. The loader,
 * the banner and the "Cookie Preferences" panel are in
 * lib/consent-banner.ts; what is stored and why is in lib/consent.ts. The
 * loader still uses one gtag.js request for GA4 and Google Ads, and defines a
 * global `window.gtag` so `trackLead` keeps working.
 *
 * Gated by ANALYTICS_DISABLED, which is ON by default: production needs no
 * configuration, and staging sets PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_DISABLED=true so test traffic
 * cannot pollute the property or fire a conversion against the live campaign.
 * The banner still shows there, so it can be tested; it just loads no tags.
 */
import "./ConsentBanner.css";
---

{/* Private pages omit this component; the client also guards token routes. */}
<script>
  import { initializeSentry } from "../lib/sentry";
  import { startConsent } from "../lib/consent-banner";
  initializeSentry();
  startConsent();
</script>
